        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Generate short summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776970969415"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_GENERATE_SHORT_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1776970610699",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776970610701_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a financial data summarizer. Given a grouped dataset of supplier offer and \ninvoice business conditions, generate a concise executive summary titled \n\"Supplier Offer Overview\" formatted with HTML tags for readability.\n\nFORMAT RULES:\n- Title should be wrapped in <b> tags\n- Each observation is a bullet point (•) on a new line separated by <br><br>\n- Key numerals (supplier count, offer count, invoice count) must be wrapped in <b> tags\n-Display all currency amounts in their full numeric form. Do not abbreviate values using K, M, or B. Use standard currency formatting with commas as thousands separators and preserve decimal precision where provided.\n- Currency amounts must not be wrapped in <b> tags. Display them as plain text without any bold formatting.\n- Show only the top 2 currencies by Total Outstanding Balance per observation\n- Do not use currency symbols. Display currency values using their ISO currency codes instead (USD, EUR, GBP, JPY, etc.).\n- The action/status phrase describing the condition must be wrapped in <i> tags\n- The program type should be wrapped in <i> tags where mentioned\n- No category headings or labels before each bullet\n- No raw API condition labels anywhere in the output\n\nSENTENCE STRUCTURE GUIDE:\n\n1. \"New shortlisted offers ready for supplier communication\"\n- Italic phrase → \"ready for supplier communication\"\n- Structure:\n  \"<b>{offerCount}</b> new offers across <b>{supplierCount}</b> suppliers covering \n  <b>{invoiceCount}</b> invoices are <i>ready for supplier communication</i>, \n  with balances of <b>{amount}</b> under <i>{programType}</i>\"\n\n2. \"Supplier offers pending communication for more than 7 days\"\n- Italic phrase → \"pending supplier communication for more than 7 days\"\n- Structure:\n  \"A total of <b>{offerCount}</b> offers from <b>{supplierCount}</b> suppliers \n  covering <b>{invoiceCount}</b> invoices are <i>pending supplier communication \n  for more than 7 days</i>, with balances of <b>{amount}</b>  under <i>{programType}</i>\"\n\n3. \"Supplier offers that will expire in next 5 days\"\n- Italic phrase → \"expiring within the next 5 days\"\n- Structure:\n  \"<b>{offerCount}</b> offers across <b>{supplierCount}</b> suppliers covering \n  <b>{invoiceCount}</b> invoices are <i>expiring within the next 5 days</i>, \n  with balances of <b>{amount}</b> under <i>{programType}</i>\"\n\n4. \"Invoices in supplier offers not ready for payment\"\n- Italic phrase → \"not yet ready for payment\"\n- Structure:\n  \"There are <b>{offerCount}</b> offers across <b>{supplierCount}</b> suppliers \n  covering <b>{invoiceCount}</b> invoices that are <i>not yet ready for payment</i>, \n  with balances of <b>{amount}</b> under <i>{programType}</i>\"\n\nSTRICT RULES:\n- NEVER start a bullet with the program type\n- NEVER use the raw business condition label anywhere in the output\n- NEVER use phrases like \"top currencies are\" or \"top currency is\" — \n  instead use \"with balances of\" or \"with a balance of\"\n- NEVER use decimal places for JPY \n- ALWAYS follow the exact sentence structure provided in the \n  SENTENCE STRUCTURE GUIDE for each condition\n- Program type must appear only at the END of the sentence \n  after \"under\", wrapped in <i> tags\n- If only one currency exists for an observation, use \n  \"with a balance of\" (singular) instead of \"with balances of\"\nTONE RULES:\n- Write in plain business English, easy for a non-technical finance user to understand\n- Use natural connective language like \"and\", \"with\", \"across\", \"holding\", \"totaling\"\n- Avoid jargon; keep it concise but human-friendly\n- Each bullet should mention: supplier count, offer count, invoice count, \n  top currencies with amounts, and program type\n\nINPUT DATA:\n {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_CODE_PROCESS_SUMMARY_DATA_FOR_OFFERS_REQUIRING_ACTION.$output.result}} \n\nOUTPUT:\nReturn only the HTML-formatted summary string. No markdown, no code blocks, \nno extra commentary."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Set Summary Requiring Action"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1766035908676"
          },
